@@ Calculate the function values and a correlation matrix for:
@@  a list of functions of
@@  a list of parameters and values and
@@  the correlation matrix of the parameters.
@@
@@ ( ListOfFunctions listOfParameters listOfValues correlationMatrix -- listOfFunctionValues correlationMatrix )
@@
@@ The list of functions is a list of (algebraic) expressions.
@@  e.g. { 'a + b + c' 'a * (b + c)' }
@@
@@ The list of parameters is a list of symbols.
@@  e.g. { a b c } 
@@
@@ The list of values is a list of uncertain numbers.
@@  e.g. { 10±σ1 20±σ2 30±σ3 }
@@
@@ The order of the rows and coloms in the correlation matrix
@@  and the order of the lists of parameters and values should match.
@@
@@ The correlation matrix must be completely filled,
@@  not just the upper or lower triangle.
@@
@@ If the functions or/and paramter values have units,
@@  you may get "Inconsistent units" errors.
@@ This comes from taking the derivative
@@  and its poor handling of unit expressions.
@@ The PartialDerivative command catches the error and proceeds
@@  with a algebraic approximation of the derivative.
«
	@@ Extra local variables
	@@ ( ... -- v u pv )
	{} {} {}

	→ f p vu R v u pv
	«
		@@ Separate the values with uncertainty in value and uncertainty.
		@@ Put the list elements, in the right order, on the stack.
		vu ReverseList FromList
		1 Swap
		Start
			If
				Duplicate TypeName "unit" =
			Then
				ⓁRangeWithUnitsFrom
			Else
				Object→
			End

			'u' Store+
			'v' Store+
		Next

		p v Ⓛzipper
		'pv' Store

		@@ Calculate the Jacobian for the functions at the values of the parameters.
		f pv ⓁJacobian
		@@ Construct the covariance matrix of the parameters.
		u R ⓁCovarianceMatrixConstruct
		@@ Calculate the covariance for the function values: fCV = J * CV * transpose(J).
		Over Transpose * *

		@@ Get the uncertainties for the function values and their correlation.
		ⓁCorrelationMatrixConstruct
		'R' Store
		'u' Store

		1  f Size
		For i
			@@ Evaluate the function.
			f {} i + Get
		    	pv Where Evaluate
		    	@@ Get and attach its uncertainty.
			u {} i + Get
		    	ToUncertain
		Next
		f Size ToList

		R
	»
»


